       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg daily is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or CNS toxicity. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that limit.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Usual adult dosing is:\n- **Depression, OCD, or other indications:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily.\n- **Titration:** increase in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of at least one week.\n- **Maximum:** 200 mg once daily.\n\nPlease confirm one of these:\n1. **A different dose**, such as 50, 100, or 200 mg daily. I'll enter it right away.\n2. **600 mg is intended.** I'd need your confirmation and a clinical rationale for the order note. Pharmacy will probably want to review it too.\n\nWhich would you like?"
